  "description": "\u201cTriangles which are on the same base and in the same parallels are equal to one another.\u201d\n\u2014 Euclid's Elements, BOOK I \u2022 PROP. 37 (G.66)\n\n00:00 1 \u00b7 GIVEN: \u27e8 A B C \u27e9, \u27e8 D B C \u27e9 (/ A D / \u2225 / B C /)\n00:19 2 \u00b7 CONSTRUCT: extend(/ A D /) \u2192 / E A /, / D F /\n00:26 3 \u00b7 CONSTRUCT: parallel_line(B, / C A /) \u2192 / B E /, parallel_line(C, / B D /) \u2192 / C F /\n00:33 4 \u00b7 ASSERT: / B C / \u2225 / E F /, / B E / \u2225 / C A /, / B D / \u2225 / C F / \u2192 \u27e8 E B C A \u27e9 = \u27e8 D B C F \u27e9\n00:47 5 \u00b7 ASSERT: \u27e8 E A B \u27e9 = \u27e8 A B C \u27e9, \u27e8 D B C \u27e9 = \u27e8 F D C \u27e9\n01:00 6 \u00b7 \u2234: \u27e8 A B C \u27e9 = \u27e8 D B C \u27e9\n\nGEOMETOR \u2022 G.66 \u2022 v2",
